-# Public Gmail drafts
-
-The public demo uses its own Google Web application client ID, registered only for https://www.cafe-replenishment-demo.com. The ID is public configuration in public-config.json; no client secret belongs in this browser integration. build_pages.py validates it and emits dist/demo/public-config.js.
-
-Open Settings → Your Gmail drafts. The first connection click loads the official Google Identity Services SDK. A second explicit Authorize click opens Google's account and consent popup. Each visitor chooses their own account. The application requests openid, email and gmail.compose, verifies actual grants, then requests the verified account email and subject identifier. gmail.compose includes the ability to send mail, but the only Gmail operation implemented here is POST /gmail/v1/users/me/drafts. The application never sends email or imports the inbox.
-
-Access tokens and account identity stay in this tab's memory; no access or refresh token enters localStorage, sessionStorage, application logs, Netlify functions or deployment artifacts. This browser flow does not request a refresh token. Reconnect through Google if access expires. The separate local installed application has its own automatic refresh implementation and is unaffected.
-
-After approving a simulated procurement list, expand one supplier and choose Review Gmail draft. Check the destination Google account, reserved example.com recipient, translated subject and body; tick the confirmation and save once. MIME uses UTF-8, CRLF, a From address bound to the authenticated account and a Date header. Account, supplier, approved order, contents and language are bound to the preview. Edits or language changes invalidate it. The operation is locked before POST. Unknown outcomes stay locked in that tab; check Gmail before any reload. Definite 4xx errors require a fresh preview. Locks persist through reconnect in the same tab but cannot prevent duplicates across reloads, devices or separate tabs.
-
-Disconnect clears the tab connection. Revoke additionally requests Google revocation and reports uncertainty; Google Account third-party connections remains available. Existing Gmail drafts are not deleted.
-
-The Google app is currently unverified. The consent warning and Google unverified-user limits apply. Creating the client does not complete Google's review. Do not describe this deployment as approved for unlimited public Gmail users.
-
-Offline verification: node --test tests/gmail-public.test.mjs. All provider requests in these tests are fakes. Real consent must be completed by the account holder and any live draft creation must use the reviewed approved simulation. No email is sent.
-
-References: https://developers.google.com/identity/oauth2/web/guides/use-token-model ; https://developers.google.com/workspace/gmail/api/guides/drafts ; https://developers.google.com/workspace/gmail/api/auth/scopes
