-# Optional personal 360dialog sandbox — published 2026-10-23
-
-This addition is an independent optional exploration path. It does not bypass,
-unlock, migrate or replace a restricted Meta WABA. Existing Meta approved-template
-validation remains unchanged. Offline implementation/testing made no provider calls. Production deployment
-6ada3c48d3b2d6d4dc5c321c published both independent functions. The public
-verification checked 22 static hashes and four function rejection boundaries;
-both durable conditional-store probes passed. No public provider send was made.
-A separate private desktop test sent one approved simulated purchase; the owner
-confirmed receipt, while the provider response remained unknown and the resend
-lock stayed in place. This is user confirmation, not a signed delivery webhook.
-
-## Scope
-
-- Only the visitor's own key and its fixed own phone number or BSUID.
-- Official fixed HTTPS endpoint: https://waba-sandbox.360dialog.io/v1/messages
-- Key is sent in D360-API-KEY, never a URL. Redirects are refused; no owner key,
-  environment fallback, automatic provider fallback or automatic POST retry.
-- API key and bound recipient live only in the current tab. Reload/Clear removes
-  credentials; they are never added to localStorage, simulation state or audit logs.
-- Preview submits credentials to this site's function, never the provider. It
-  binds hashed configuration, exact recipient, language and purchase parameters
-  in Netlify Blobs. A separate confirmation is required for the actual send.
-- Local simulated approval and own-recipient / last-24-hours assertions are user
-  declarations. The server binds this payload, but cannot independently verify
-  those facts. The provider enforces its own fixed-recipient/conversation rules.
-- Messages are visibly marked as simulated purchases, not real supplier orders.
-- 201 plus one safe message ID means accepted only. No inbound/status webhook or
-  external tunnel has been configured; there is no automatic delivered claim.
-- Network, provider, malformed response or record uncertainty remains unknown.
-  A conditional persistent send claim blocks matching resends across instances,
-  changed request/preview IDs, key rotation and language changes. Do not delete
-  send records to retry an uncertain request.
-
-## Budget and retention
-
-Official sandbox documentation currently describes free access with at most 200
-requests per key, including rejected requests. This is the provider quota, not a
-hard cap on this website's function calls or storage. Preview does not consume a
-provider message request, but does consume hosting resources.
-
-The new function limits traffic to 10 requests per minute across the production
-site domain. It uses the existing Netlify Free plan and existing Blobs dependency;
-no paid plan, recurring add-on, auto-recharge, scheduled job or purchased number is
-introduced. Free quota exhaustion can pause the site; do not enable paid upgrades
-as a workaround. A hosting platform's plan quota is separate from API rate limits.
-
-Preview records expire for sending after 15 minutes, but are not automatically
-deleted from Blobs. They retain only hashes/status/expiry, not keys, phone numbers
