-    'An advanced test option lets you use your own Meta business account and temporary access token. Credentials remain only in the current tab memory; reloading clears them. Each request passes the token, sender and recipient numbers, approved template and selected purchase summary through this site’s Netlify Function to Meta. They are not shared with other visitors or sent to the local owner workbench. The function does not persist the token, raw numbers or message body. Netlify Blobs stores hashed send keys, request and claim IDs, timestamps, acceptance status and Meta message IDs to prevent duplicate sends. Hosting request metadata may be logged separately. Unknown outcomes stay blocked and are not automatically retried; clearing browser state does not remove these server-side duplicate guards. Do not enter confidential business information. This is a bring-your-own-token testing option, not an approved Embedded Signup connection for arbitrary businesses. Removing a token here does not revoke it at Meta or delete delivered messages.',
